      "bottomRightX": 677,
      "bottomRightY": 249,
      "content": "The de Broglie wave length will be given by $h / \\lambda = p = |\\mathfrak{p}| = \\frac{h}{2\\pi}k$. The solution (8) should be regarded as normalized in the sense of taking the mean [see (2), § 2]. We briefly denote a function of $x, y, t$ by $f(\\mathfrak{r})$, a function of $k_x, k_y, k_z$ by $f(\\mathfrak{k})$, etc. Let $dS = dx dy dz$.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
